  "summary": "Ignore BIP35 mempool messages from peers that have transaction relay disabled (fRelay=false), unless the connection has the mempool net permission. Peers can still obtain mempool inventory after enabling transaction relay, such as by sending a BIP37 filterload message, which subjects them to existing inbound transaction-relay connection limits.",
  "problem": "When a node runs with bloom filtering enabled, an inbound peer can connect with fRelay=false to evade the inbound transaction-relay connection capacity limits introduced in PR 28463, while still requesting and receiving full mempool inventory via BIP35 mempool messages.",
