  "card": "Bitcoin Core now ignores BIP35 mempool requests from peers that have transaction relay disabled, unless they are granted the mempool network permission. Currently, inbound peers can connect with fRelay=false to avoid counting toward the inbound transaction-relay capacity limit added in PR 28463, yet still consume bandwidth by requesting full mempool inventory. Requiring active transaction relay closes this loophole while preserving SPV clients like bitcoinj that send a BIP37 filterload message before requesting the mempool.",
